Proposed (94.0s): Use this skill for any web information need — URLs, websites, online lookups, or external sources. Five intents: (1) web search for articles, news, papers, or facts on any topic; (2) URL extraction — readable text from a specific page (Wikipedia, docs, JS-heavy SPAs); (3) site crawl — bulk-download pages from a docs section or domain as markdown; (4) URL discovery — list all URLs under a domain path; (5) cited research — multi-source report with sources. Especially useful when the user wants curated, filtered output (titles, scores, specific numbers, key paragraphs) rather than raw HTML flooding context — process results through Python so only relevant fields enter context. Trigger on 'search', 'look up', 'find articles', 'fetch this page', 'extract content', 'crawl docs', 'discover URLs', 'research with sources', and equivalents in any language (搜一下 / 查一下 / 提取 / 爬取 / 研究). Do NOT trigger for local file ops, git, code editing, local JSON parsing, or local scripts.

